= Discussion and Limitations

// OUTLINE ONLY.

- What the evidence does not reach: measured results are machine- and
  version-specific (Zen5 confound as the worked example); proofs are in a
  model, not on silicon (layers A–D vocabulary keeps these apart).
- Model-blocked steps: the two parallel Polygeist passes; what unblocking
  would take.
- The compiler-removed surprise: compilation is not monotonically bad for
  confidentiality — implications for "compile with hardening" guidance.
- Generalizing past Polygeist/Inductor: what transfers via the shared
  dialects, what is compiler-specific.
- Ethics: no deployed-system exploitation; all measurement on our own
  hardware and models.
